        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a745a4ce-abff-518a-8669-fb5b647bd428",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Publications: Woman's Day, The Lady, The Queen, Beyond Black & White, Ebony, Jet, Reuters\n- Companies: The Great Atlantic & Pacific Tea Company, Hearst Corporation\n- People: Christelyn Karazin, Nora Shackleton Heald\n- Places: London\n- Roles: journalist, editor\n\nFacts:\n- The Lady has been in continuous publication since 1885 and is based in London.\n- Nora Shackleton Heald, born in 1882, was a British journalist.\n- Woman's Day was first published in 1931 by The Great Atlantic & Pacific Tea Company.\n- Nora Shackleton Heald was editor of The Queen and later The Lady from at least as early as 1948 until 1954.\n- Nora Shackleton Heald died on 5 April 1961.\n- The Lady is Britain's longest-running weekly women's magazine.\n- Christelyn Karazin hosts the blog Beyond Black & White.\n- Christelyn Karazin has written for Woman's Day, Ebony, Jet, and Reuters.\n- Hearst Corporation is the current publisher of Woman's Day.",
